From 1416f157f0c7ca3953162b6d0aa15267c9c021ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 18:55:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: A22X auto-route deadlock-prone GMEM batches to
 sysmem (high draw count on multi-tile FB)

On A22X (Adreno 220/225) the EDRAM back-end deadlocks
(RBBM_STATUS=0xc4010310, all of GUI+RB+VGT+CP_NRT busy + CP cmd FIFO
1/16 free, no progress) on high-aggregate-work batches that span
multiple GMEM tiles -- e.g. shadow-mapping passes that issue many
draws into a 1024x768 framebuffer that needs 2+ tiles on the A220's
512 KB GMEM.

Auto-route those batches to sysmem so the deadlock-prone GMEM tile
machinery is skipped.

Heuristic
---------

  pixels >= 512 * 512 && num_draws >= 25

The pixels threshold picks framebuffers that need at least two GMEM
tiles (32 bpp color + depth fits ~2 tiles at 512x512 on A220's GMEM).
The num_draws threshold of 25 was empirically tuned: webOS surface-
manager's heaviest steady-state batches are num_draws=13 on 1024x768
and complete cleanly in GMEM, while glmark2 desktop:effect=shadow
w=4 produces num_draws=25-50 batches that DO hit the deadlock and
benefit from sysmem (was 26 fps + hang in GMEM; 71 fps under sysmem).

Why not also auto-route batch->restore != 0
-------------------------------------------

An earlier revision of this heuristic auto-routed any batch with
batch->restore != 0 (FBO read-back, multi-pass compositing) to
sysmem, intending to catch glmark2 desktop:effect=blur w=4's ping-
pong composite (restore=0x4 = PIPE_CLEAR_COLOR0). That clause also
caught webOS surface-manager / luna-next-cardshell's status bar,
card-thumbnail and lock-screen compositing batches -- which use the
same restore=0x4 bit because both are color-attachment-0 read-backs
indistinguishable at the freedreno layer.

Routing the cardshell batches through sysmem produced an intermittent
failure mode for surface-manager's specific draw shape that the GMEM
path handles cleanly -- the user-visible regression was tap and
swipe gestures not propagating to the UI because the compositor was
repeatedly producing intermittently-bad frames. Validated 2026-06-03
on a kernel-side bisect spanning 12 days of changes (drm/msm core +
a2xx rebuild, mmcc-msm8660 sashiko fixes, gdsc Set A iterations
v2..v6, GPU DVFS / kgsl_style_boost, autosuspend force-reset path):
NONE of the kernel suspects were the regression. Reverting just this
Mesa patch restored cardshell gesture responsiveness across the
whole UI.

The restore mask cannot tell blur from surface-manager apart, so the
restore-based clause is omitted. glmark2 desktop:effect=blur w=4 may
deadlock in GMEM again under this heuristic; run with
FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem to force it through the sysmem path for those
edge cases. Daily-driver compositing on the same hardware now works
correctly.

FD_MESA_DEBUG=gmem forces GMEM for debug; FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem
forces sysmem unconditionally.

Validation table
----------------

  surface-manager / luna-next-cardshell:           GMEM, gestures OK
  jellyfish (1024x768, num_draws=2):                GMEM, 12 fps
  glmark2 build/shading/bump (num_draws=1):         GMEM, Success
  binner_test heavy (256x256 batches, num_draws=1): GMEM
  glmark2 desktop:shadow w=4 (1024x768, num_draws=25-50): sysmem, 71 fps
  glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 (1024x768, restore=0x4): GMEM (may
    deadlock; use FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem to force)

Requires the sysmem-prep correctness fixes (RB_DEPTH_INFO emit + skip
HW fast-clear under sysmem) to be in place, otherwise auto-routed
batches would render garbage.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 .../drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c        | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
index a5ea50ad9eb..449cfb15057 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "freedreno_gmem.h"
 #include "freedreno_query_hw.h"
 #include "freedreno_resource.h"
+#include "freedreno_screen.h"
 #include "freedreno_tracepoints.h"
 #include "freedreno_util.h"
 
@@ -780,6 +781,54 @@ fd_gmem_render_tiles(struct fd_batch *batch)
       if ((pfb->nr_cbufs == 0) && !pfb->zsbuf.texture) {
          sysmem = true;
       }
+
+      /* A22X (Adreno 220/225) GMEM-deadlock heuristic:
+       *
+       * On A22X the EDRAM back-end deadlocks (RBBM_STATUS=0xc4010310, all of
+       * GUI+RB+VGT+CP_NRT busy + CP cmd FIFO 1/16 free, no progress) on
+       * high-aggregate-work batches on multi-tile FBOs (shadow mapping,
+       * complex scenes) where num_draws across many tiles saturates the
+       * EDRAM back-end pipeline. Empirically a 1024x768 batch with >=25
+       * draws is sufficient to hit it on A220.
+       *
+       * Earlier revisions of this heuristic also auto-routed batches with
+       * batch->restore != 0 (FBO read-back, multi-pass compositing) to
+       * sysmem, intending to catch glmark2 desktop:effect=blur w=4's
+       * ping-pong composite. That clause also caught webOS surface-manager
+       * / luna-next-cardshell's status bar and card-thumbnail compositing
+       * batches (restore=0x4 = PIPE_CLEAR_COLOR0, same as blur's
+       * indistinguishable bit), and the sysmem path has an intermittent
+       * failure mode for surface-manager's specific draw shape that the
+       * GMEM path handles cleanly -- the user-visible regression was
+       * tap/swipe gestures not propagating to the UI because the
+       * compositor was repeatedly producing intermittently-bad frames.
+       * The restore mask cannot distinguish blur from surface-manager, so
+       * the auto-route based on restore is dropped. glmark2 blur w=4 may
+       * deadlock in GMEM again under this heuristic; run with
+       * FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem to force it through the sysmem path for
+       * those edge cases.
+       *
+       * Single-draw and few-draw, full-clear batches (build/shading/bump/
+       * texture, surface-manager, binner_test heavy, jellyfish) keep GMEM
+       * tile speed. !FD_DBG(GMEM) so users can force GMEM for debug.
+       *
+       * Validated 2026-06-03:
+       *   surface-manager / luna-next-cardshell:           GMEM, gestures OK
+       *   jellyfish (1024x768, num_draws=2):                GMEM, 12 fps
+       *   glmark2 build/shading/bump (num_draws=1):         GMEM, Success
+       *   binner_test heavy (256x256 batches, num_draws=1): GMEM
+       *   glmark2 desktop:shadow w=4 (1024x768, num_draws=25-50): sysmem
+       *   glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 (1024x768, restore=0x4): GMEM (may
+       *     deadlock; use FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem to force)
+       *
+       * 512*512 ~ 2 tiles on A220's 512KB GMEM (32bpp color + depth).
+       */
+      if (is_a22x(ctx->screen) && !FD_DBG(GMEM)) {
+         const unsigned pixels = pfb->width * pfb->height;
+         if (pixels >= 512 * 512 && batch->num_draws >= 25) {
+            sysmem = true;
+         }
+      }
    }
 
    if (FD_DBG(SYSMEM))
